# One regex per line. Keep entries narrow and explain the CSS-variable source.
# chart-core.ts has no getComputedStyle-derived canvas colors in Wave 1, so it
# intentionally has no allowlist entry yet.

# Wave 3 A1: readChartPalette() in chart-core.ts reads live CSS custom
# properties via getComputedStyle and only falls back to these hex literals
# when a --joy-* variable is unset (e.g. non-browser test environments).
# These are JS default-argument literals, not un-token-driven CSS, so they
# are intentionally allowlisted narrowly to this call shape. Entries are
# scoped to chart-core.ts by anchoring on the "<path>:<line>:" prefix that
# lint-colors.sh's rg hit lines carry, so no other file can ride on them.
(^|/)chart-core\.ts:[0-9]+:.*v\('--joy-[a-z-]+', '#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,8}'\)

# Wave 3 A1 (RXD-010 close-out): chart-core.ts grid-line and crosshair-line
# strokeStyle assignments that ternary-branch on isDark/theme between two
# rgba(...) translucent-overlay literals. A single opacity value is not
# representable as one semantic token, and these already branch correctly
# per theme, so they are legitimate theme-branching translucent strokes, not
# un-tokenized CSS.
(^|/)chart-core\.ts:[0-9]+:.*ctx\.strokeStyle = .*\? 'rgba\([0-9, .]+\)' : 'rgba\([0-9, .]+\)'
